# Buddy The Underwriter — git attributes
#
# docs/commissioning/BUDDY_CONTINUOUS_COMMISSIONING_LEDGER.md is a shared,
# append-at-EOF document. Every commissioning PR used to add its own section at
# the end, so any merge to main made every other open PR conflict on the same
# final line. In one 19-PR batch that cascade fired six times and produced ~80
# hand-resolved conflicts, none of which involved disagreeing content: both
# sides were always adding, never changing the same text.
#
# `merge=union` is git's built-in resolution for exactly that shape. It keeps
# both sides' added lines instead of raising a conflict.
#
# TRADE-OFF, read before adding files here: a union-merged file NEVER reports a
# conflict. That is correct for a file that is only ever appended to, and wrong
# for one where two branches might revise the same existing text — such a revision
# would be silently duplicated rather than flagged. The ledger is append-only by
# convention (see docs/commissioning/README.md), which is what makes this safe.
# Editing a historical ledger entry on two branches at once is the one case this
# will not protect you from; do such edits on a single branch.
#
# Do not extend union merging to source files.
docs/commissioning/BUDDY_CONTINUOUS_COMMISSIONING_LEDGER.md merge=union
